// The values in this closure share structure: every round, `xs` contains the
// previous round's function many times. Computing the depth by walking the
// value as a tree would visit it exponentially often, so the depth check would
// hang instead of reporting the error.
{[]}.transitive_closure(b => let xs = [for _ in std.range(0, 64): b]; [() => xs])

